Process observation and signal methods use the control mailbox while a caller waits for exit in the application mailbox.
Classify only builtin Process reads, inspector metadata and signal sends this way; ordinary objects and Process launch/configuration retain serialized dispatch.
Initialize each Process state exactly once; read its started/running state under its state lock.

Terminal and Pipeline wrappers route observation, terminal input/resize and stop signals through the control mailbox as well.
Their wrapper methods delegate straight to Process so nested self control sends cannot deadlock the lane.
Process terminal cursor reads and pipeline stage exits remain observable during wait.
